Design an in-memory Task Scheduler (similar to Java’s ScheduledThreadPoolExecutor).
Requirements:
Support scheduling one-time tasks to execute after a given delay.
Support scheduling recurring tasks to execute periodically at fixed intervals.
Support canceling a scheduled task before it executes.
Ensure the design is thread-safe so multiple clients can submit tasks concurrently.
Optimize for CPU usage (prevent busy-waiting/spinning when worker threads have no immediate tasks).
Ensure fault tolerance (if a client's task throws an exception, it should not crash the worker thread).


Entities:

Task: class
run()

TaskType: enum
onetime, recurring

scheduledTask: class implement Comparable

WorkerThread: class

TaskScheduler: class

ThreadPool: class
Queue<WorkerThread> threads
addThreadToQueue(WorkerThread workerThread)
pollFromQueue(WorkerThread workerThread)

ScheduledThreadPoolExecutor: class